76
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:25,200
Thank you, Kahono.

77
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:27,200
A thousand mules should cover it.

78
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:31,200
I'll give you a hundred times that if we survive.

79
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:35,200
Now, we need to get the others on their feet.

80
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:38,200
Can you use your recovery magic?

81
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,200
Well, I can.

82
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:44,200
But do you really think he'll wait until I'm done singing to attack?

83
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,200
What's that?

84
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,200
Who's he?

85
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,200
Hey!

86
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,200
Big Brother!

87
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:58,200
Why the heck are you sleeping?

88
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:01,200
We got a promise to keep, remember?

89
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:05,200
We're never gonna get famous if we let this beast man kill us!

90
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:10,200
Did you forget about our singing-dancing brother-sister act?!

91
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,200
No, of course I didn't!

92
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,200
Wait, Big Brother?

93
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:17,200
Yep, that good-for-nothing dumb-dumb over there is my Big Brother Kyoto.

94
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:19,200
Who are you calling good-for-nothing?!

95
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:25,200
If I hadn't deflected the force of that punch with my dance magic,

96
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:27,200
I'd be missing a head right now.

97
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:30,200
It'll be impossible to beat, but-

98
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:32,200
My brother and I have a dream.

99
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,200
We're gonna go ashore someday!

100
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,200
Yeah, that's right!

101
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:37,200
We can't give up now!

102
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:39,200
We won't let our dream die!

103
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:40,200
Let's go!

104
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:41,200
Yeah!

105
00:05:49,200 --> 00:06:00,200
I can feel it!

106
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,200
The Mon is getting stronger!

107
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,200
Combo spell!

108
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,200
Now Seagod Slash!

109
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:13,200
Compound magic that combines song and dance.

110
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:16,200
Kahano's singing enhances my dance magic,

111
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:20,200
allowing me to release enormous strikes of magic power at the enemy!

112
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,200
That's it!

113
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,200
Come on!

114
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,200
You're doing well!

115
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:41,200
You can defeat him, I know you can!

116
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,200
Ever since you were little,

117
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:45,200
you've both worked so hard to make your dreams come true!

118
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:51,200
unexpected music

119
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,200
That oughta'a be enough practicing for today, don't you think?

120
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,200
Nuh ahm.

121
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,200
If you wanna be rich someday,

122
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,200
you gotta try harder than that!

123
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:13,200
I guess you're right.

124
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,200
Becoming a star dancer is tough.

125
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:18,460
Yeah. And besides, we don't just want to be famous.

126
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:20,640
We want to please the sea god, too.

127
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:22,740
We've got a lot of work to do.

128
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:25,100
Kay, you ready?

129
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:26,160
Mm-hmm.

130
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:40,760
Hard work will never betray you.

131
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:51,160
A sparrow's song and a waltzing mouse.

132
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:53,300
I wouldn't expect them to be so powerful.

133
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:57,200
They have some unique spells for living in such a remote location.

134
00:07:57,880 --> 00:08:00,480
That's right. This place is what shaped our magic.

135
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:04,160
It's been woven into the very fabric of our lives.

136
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:08,300
Generations of our people have praised the sea god with their singing and dancing.

137
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:12,020
We've been practicing all of our lives.

138
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:15,280
Each song and each dance is an offering to the sea god,

139
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:17,540
to him, and to everyone we love.

140
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:21,000
This magic bonds the people of the underwater temple.

141
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:30,360
You've got him now, Kij! Take the beast out!

142
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:32,160
We'll never let that bond be broken!

143
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:34,360
You won't defeat us!

144
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:40,180
Did it work?

145
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:47,660
Done with your little speech now.

146
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:51,260
There's no way!

147
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:02,060
Keep trying.

148
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:17,120
Kiato!

149
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:17,400
Kiato!

150
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,500
Kiato!

151
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:29,180
Run now!

152
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:30,060
Kahuno!

153
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:32,720
Dreams and bombs.

154
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,800
What do humans know of those?

155
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:38,140
Don't speak such words to me, girl!

156
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:43,180
Kahuno!

157
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:50,520
All right, you beast.

158
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:51,820
Now game magic.

159
00:09:52,020 --> 00:09:52,860
Monster time!

160
00:09:52,860 --> 00:10:00,100
Can't you muster anything beyond a childish diversion?

161
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:15,720
We had those months as well, our own dreams and bombs, until you humans destroyed them!

162
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:23,780
We, the Eye of the Midnight Sun, had golden dreams and bombs of blood!

163
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:25,360
I don't understand!

164
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,940
What is he babbling on about, damnable rabid beast monster?

165
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:36,220
It looks like there will be no more singing and dancing for the two of you.

166
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:41,600
All it took was a couple of well-timed strikes to crush those silly dreams of yours.

167
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,660
What good are you now?

168
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:45,780
You're a sparrow without a voice.

169
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,680
The very essence of despair.

170
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,000
How delicious.

171
00:10:49,000 --> 00:11:00,760
So there's still a scrap of defiance left in you, is there?

172
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:02,520
Very well.

173
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:06,220
Let's see how you'll feel after I tear your wings off.

174
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:08,660
Really?

175
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:11,980
A sparrow that can't sing has no reason to live anyway.

176
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:13,720
I think I'll just...

177
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,600
Don't touch her!

178
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:18,760
Put her down!

179
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:20,660
Do it right now!

180
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:24,380
You truly think I'll stop because you told me to?

181
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:29,700
If I miss, I might hit Kahono.

182
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:34,180
You and your worthless friends never had a chance of defeating me.

183
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,280
Go on.

184
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:36,340
Howl.

185
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:38,060
Embrace your despair!

186
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:41,580
I couldn't bring myself to attack then either.

187
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:45,460
Would my attacks even do anything against someone like that?

188
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:47,120
No one else's have.

189
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:55,880
If you're not going to use that thing, then just stand there and watch.

190
00:11:56,260 --> 00:11:57,720
Watch her die.

191
00:11:57,720 --> 00:12:09,120
Everyone else's fought until they're too exhausted or hurt to go on.

192
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:11,860
But I...

193
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:13,220
I just can't.

194
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:18,820
It's alright.

195
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:22,620
Kahono!

196
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,760
There's a great power within you.

197
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:30,940
You're strong enough to handle it now.

198
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:35,860
Because you're fighting to protect what's precious to you.

199
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,160
You're fighting to win, Noelle.

200
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,820
What's precious to me...

201
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:47,460
It will be alright.

202
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,040
Don't doubt it.

203
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:52,080
Because I say so, and I'm your friend.

204
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:16,500
What's happening?

205
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:18,100
It's shaking.

206
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:22,080
What is this?

207
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:23,940
It's about time, Noelle.

208
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:26,220
Get him.

209
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,800
I won't tell you again.

210
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:33,240
Where did all this power come from?

211
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:37,580
Release my friend at once, or you'll regret it!

212
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:45,640
Tell me, Black Bull girl.

213
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:49,740
You aren't hesitating because of your sibling's taunting, are you?

214
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:54,120
There's no time for that on the battlefield!

215
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:58,160
One bad decision out here could mean lives lost.

216
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:00,100
Forget your insecurities.

217
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:03,300
You stand here today as a member of the Magic Knights.

218
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:09,120
If you join the order of your own accord, you must be determined to grow stronger.

219
00:14:10,460 --> 00:14:11,020
Stronger?

220
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:14,060
There isn't any shame in being weak, girl.

221
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,800
The shame is in staying weak.

222
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:30,800
Release my friend at once, or you'll regret it!

223
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,560
So strong.

224
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:34,340
Who is this girl?

225
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:35,300
Hold on.

226
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,520
Are you royalty?

227
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,900
And what does it matter if I am?

228
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:41,180
That isn't what's important to me right now!

229
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:44,240
I am Noelle Silva of the Black Bulls!

230
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:48,660
And I'm done standing by and watching while you hurt my friends and squadmates!

231
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:50,420
I see.

232
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:51,920
So it's true.

233
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:55,240
A member of the human's most corrupt class.

234
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:55,840
Good.

235
00:14:55,840 --> 00:15:08,280
I'll make an example of you.

236
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:12,440
Now hit me with everything you've got, you disgusting royal parasite!

237
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:16,820
Oh, I was planning on it!

238
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,860
I'll show you the power of a royal parasite!

239
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:21,880
Water creation magic!

240
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,780
Sea dragons roar!

241
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:38,860
Sea Claw!

242
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,220
Sea Claw!

243
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:01,360
One!

244
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:05,980
Terra!

245
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:06,640
Terra!

246
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:06,700
Terra!

247
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:07,240
Terra!

248
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:07,500
Terra!

249
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:18,840
Is... is that the Sea God?

250
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:35,340
My arm!

251
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:40,200
How's that?

252
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:42,200
Some crazy power you've got.

253
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:44,480
You really did push past those limits.

254
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:46,580
Maybe a little too far past them.

255
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:47,920
Who is that girl?

256
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:49,700
Is she the Sea Goddess?

257
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:54,380
I always figured her latent abilities were nothing to sneeze at.

258
00:16:54,980 --> 00:16:57,780
But who knew she was an attack mage all this time?

259
00:16:57,780 --> 00:17:11,740
Let us live together.

260
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:17,200
It is not you who should be despairing, but the people of the Clover Kingdom.

261
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:21,800
You must remember your true self.

262
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:27,780
Congratulations to the happy couple!

263
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:45,700
Is this...

264
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:46,500
It can't be!

265
00:17:46,660 --> 00:17:46,980
Humans?

266
00:17:46,980 --> 00:18:06,960
I'll kill you.

267
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:32,140
You have my gratitude for summoning me, human.

268
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:35,260
Where'd that eye come from?

269
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:38,640
I've never felt such sinister magic power before!

270
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:41,040
Mythical Beats Magic.

271
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:43,120
Last Endless Man!

272
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:57,680
His arm... grew back?

273
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:59,480
How is that possible?

274
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:00,700
It shouldn't be.

275
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:02,560
Not growing back a whole missing arm.

276
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:04,620
There's no spell that can do that.

277
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:08,420
Nothing to the strongest recovery magic can regenerate a limb.

278
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:11,160
At the very most, it could only hope to close up the wound.

